# an-island — plan 25 M3's NEGATIVE control, and it is the reason the
# headline gate means anything.
#
# ⚠⚠ `other == 0` over `the-ground` is satisfied by a frame with no
# background in it — which is what that fixture arranges — but it is ALSO
# satisfied by a gate that cannot see background at all.  If the clear
# colour were a palette colour, or if `classify_canvas` were bucketing
# everything, `other` would read 0 for a reason that has nothing to do
# with the ground being drawn correctly.
#
# So: the same camera, over a world far too small to fill the frame.
# `other` must come out LARGE, and every one of those pixels must be
# EXACTLY the clear colour.  Two facts in one fixture —
#
#   other > 0                the instrument can see a non-palette pixel
#   other == clear pixels    and what it is seeing is the background,
#                            not drift in the ground it did draw
#
# ⚠ The second is what makes `the-ground`'s reading a statement about
# COLOUR EXACTNESS rather than about framing.  `probe/m3` measured the
# same thing before the phase was written; this keeps it measured.

echo an-island: a patch too small to fill the frame

at 0 0 1

palette 5
drag -3 -2 3 -2
drag -3 -1 3 -1
drag -3  0 3  0
drag -3  1 3  1
drag -3  2 3  2

palette 9
click 0 0

kind  0  0 wall
kind  3  2 grass
kind 12  0 sea
